  "verbalization": "The visible evidence strongly suggests a direct relationship between Jerantinine B and HuT78, mediated through the protein Thioredoxin, mitochondrial. This pathway is supported by three distinct but overlapping connections, all pointing to Thioredoxin, mitochondrial as a common target of Jerantinine B. The protein Thioredoxin, mitochondrial is also a target of three different compounds: 5-Hydroxy-2-Methylchromone-7-O-Rutinoside, Uvaol-3-Caffeate, and Rhetsinine, all of which have a final score of 0.5484, indicating a high level of confidence in their relationship with HuT78. The consistent targeting of Thioredoxin, mitochondrial by multiple compounds suggests a potential mechanism of action involving this protein, possibly through redox regulation or other cellular processes. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of Thioredoxin, mitochondrial as a central node in the biological network linking Jerantinine B to HuT78.",
